# Line endings.
#
# Git stores LF in the repository and, without instruction, checks out CRLF on
# Windows. That is invisible until someone on macOS or Linux — or the Vercel
# build, which runs on Linux — touches the same file, at which point the diff
# shows every line as changed and review becomes impossible.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF both in the repository and in the working
# copy, on every platform. Every tool in this project (Node, Vite, the editors
# people use) handles LF natively on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never apply line-ending conversion to binary content: it corrupts the file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
